From 67748d0a9dd49c52cfab20b45f526a83dbeb119a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 02:51:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bring the bid controls and weekly fixtures to the Mock Draft
 too

The Mock Draft runs its own copy of the auction board, so none of the
draft-room work showed up there: it still had the two bare number fields
and a "Submit Bid" button, and week lines with no fixture. That is the
screen it is easiest to open, which made the changes look like they had
never landed.

Rather than a third copy of the same markup, the bid controls and the
fixture formatter move to web/src/draftControls.jsx and both pages import
them. Mock Draft picks up the steppers, the minimum-bid default, Enter to
submit, the priced button, and "vs KC" / "@ KC" / "BYE" beside each week.

Also drops the three .patch files that were committed by accident.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sdnuo56mhnsF6pDMCCDm3h
