- blank crests
-MIME-Version: 1.0
-Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
-Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
-
-Switching tabs threw people out of the draft room because supabase-js
-re-emits SIGNED_IN on routine session recovery — including every time the
-tab becomes visible again — and the auth handler routed every SIGNED_IN
-back to Home. It now compares the session's user id against who we already
-consider signed in, so only a genuinely new login changes the view.
-
-Leaving the draft and coming back showed an empty roster panel: signings
-were only fetched during the 'winners' phase, so re-entering mid-round had
-nothing to render. Rosters now load when the room opens as well.
-
-Every team but your own flew an anonymous grey shield. Teams and profiles
-are both publicly readable, so the room now fetches each team's owner crest
-once and resolves every shield — nominations, live bids, won players, the
-team switcher — through a single crestFor() helper.
-
-Also:
-- Auto-start no longer acts on the shared session's *default* 'pending'
-  phase before the real row has loaded, which could restart a draft already
-  in progress, and it retries every 10s instead of once a second. Adds a
-  commissioner override button.
-- The draft closes out once every team is either roster-full or under a
-  dollar of cap for the week. The client makes that call, since the
-  bye-week and interest math lives here; draft-end-session.sql adds the
-  RPC that makes it stick and needs running in the Supabase SQL editor.
-- Bidding no longer requires typing: the amount defaults to the minimum
-  winning bid, +/- nudge it a dollar or a week at a time, Enter submits,
-  and the button names the price.
-
-Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
