-Each week's price on a player card now names the fixture beside it — "vs KC"
-at home, "@ KC" away, "BYE" on a bye. The whole season's schedule comes from
-one query against `games`, which is already publicly readable, so this needs
-no new RPC and no migration: it's keyed by team and week and shared by every
-card on the board. Nomination cards get the same line.
-
-Team names were capped nowhere. The name field now stops at 20 characters
-with a live counter beside it, and saving trims whitespace and rejects an
-empty name, matching the 3-character cap the abbreviation already had.
-
-Team names also never updated for anyone but the person who changed them:
-the draft session stores whatever a team was called at the moment it
-nominated or bid, so a rename left stale names on every other board. Names
-now resolve from the live `teams` row by id, falling back to that snapshot
-only for a team not yet loaded, and the room subscribes to `teams` so a
-rename reaches every browser without a refresh. The roster panel is keyed by
-team id rather than team name for the same reason, which also retires
-buildMyRosterSlots — it was a duplicate of buildRosterSlotsForTeam.
